Lab: Deploy Web Applications
Objective
Deploy a reproducible web application (Famous Authors) with a MySQL backend and HTML frontend, using image streams, secrets, persistent volumes, services, and routes.
________________________________________
Project Setup
•	Project name: review
•	UI image: registry.ocp4.example.com:8443/redhattraining/famous-quotes:2-42
•	Database image stream: mysql8:1 → points to registry.ocp4.example.com:8443/rhel9/mysql-80:1-228
•	Secret for database: dbparams
user=operator1
password=redhat123
database=quotesdb
________________________________________
Step 1: Image Streams
•	Create image stream for MySQL:
oc create istag mysql8:1 --from-image registry.ocp4.example.com:8443/rhel9/mysql-80:1-228
oc set image-lookup mysql8
•	UI deployment can reference the image directly or via its own image stream.
________________________________________
Step 2: Secrets
•	Create secret for database credentials:
oc create secret generic dbparams \
  --from-literal user=operator1 \
  --from-literal password=redhat123 \
  --from-literal database=quotesdb
•	Add environment variables from secret to deployments:
oc set env deployment/mysql8 --from=secret/dbparams --prefix=MYSQL_
oc set env deployment/frontend --from=secret/dbparams \
  QUOTES_HOSTNAME=quotesdb
________________________________________
Step 3: Deployments
•	Create deployments with 0 replicas initially (scale later or triggers will handle scaling):
oc create deployment mysql8 --image=mysql8:1 --replicas=0
oc create deployment frontend --image=registry.ocp4.example.com:8443/redhattraining/famous-quotes:2-42 --replicas=0
•	Add image triggers for automatic rollout:
oc set triggers deployment/mysql8 --from-image=mysql8:1 --containers=mysql8
________________________________________
Step 4: Persistent Volumes
•	Add persistent volume to MySQL deployment:
oc set volumes deployment/mysql8 --add --claim-class=lvms-vg1 --claim-size=2Gi --mount-path=/var/lib/mysql
________________________________________
Step 5: Expose Services and Routes
•	Expose MySQL service (internal):
oc expose deployment/mysql8 --port=3306
•	Expose frontend application externally:
oc expose deployment/frontend --port=8000
oc expose service/frontend
•	Resulting route: http://frontend-review.apps.ocp4.example.com
________________________________________
Step 6: Test
•	Use curl or a browser to access the route and verify the frontend connects to the MySQL backend.
•	Update image stream tags to test automatic rollouts if new images become available.
________________________________________
Step 7: Lab Completion
•	Grade your work:
lab grade compreview-deploy
•	Finish and clean up:
lab finish compreview-deploy


